  "scope": "# Review cd818a9d92d1 \u2014 review-e9d3e60a5bb17dbe\nScope: proposed task-local parameter extension of ARC training:d9f24cd1.\nBuilt: episode-fixed left/right deflection, shared-input sampling, separate demo/query counts, and a thin promotion adapter.\nCanonical generator/rule: unchanged; right is the exact canonical Racket text. Six retained canonical pairs passed.\nBoundaries: reject edge/gray-overlap inputs, noninteger counts, duplicate inputs, retry exhaustion, and requests above the four-input 5\u00d76 support.\nVerifier repair: reject forged program/source hashes even after private data and manifest hashes are recomputed.\nEvidence: four episodes (seeds 17/29 \u00d7 left/right), two demos plus four distinct queries each; all 24 labels freshly replayed in Racket.\nTests: 19 focused prototype/adapter/adversarial tests passed; recovery-helper guards and a real private-namespace preservation probe passed.\nTickets: pinned 7cda20c438b7 overlap audit reproduced, including a lawful-size padded witness; 809c8b84e40a valid/invalid profile boundary passed.\nLimits: finite declared rival family and retained seeds; owner qualification/acceptance and training admission were not performed.\nDisposition: routine proposed prototype; existing peer overlap finding still needs owner attention. No unresolved main-prototype failures.\nCommands/hashes: RESULTS.json and checks/verification-runs.json; source patch is generated by the packet builder.",
